<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Albelda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">859</span> · Also known as Battle of Monte Laturce</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Albelda was fought in 859 near Albelda in La Rioja, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordono-i-of-asturias">Ordoño I of Asturias</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musa-ibn-musa">Musa ibn Musa</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a>, the dominant lord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-march">Upper March of al-Andalus</a>. According to the Asturian chronicles Ordoño stormed the fortress Musa was building there, and the defeat broke Musa's power. Later legend confused it with the mythical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-clavijo">Battle of Clavijo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-albelda.jpg" alt="Battle of Albelda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BigSus · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monte_Laturce.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
